}"}], "structured_content": {"result": {"id": 124764, "name": "deriv", "source_text": "/-- Derivative of `f` at the point `x`, if it exists.  Zero otherwise.

If the derivative exists (i.e., `∃ f', HasDerivAt f f' x`), then
`f x' = f x + (x' - x) • deriv f x + o(x' - x)` where `x'` converges to `x`.
-/
def deriv (f : 𝕜 → F) (x : 𝕜) :=
  fderiv 𝕜 f x 1
"}}}

